---
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
const screens = [
	{
		src: '/images/crm/screen-dashboard-en.webp',
		alt: 'Revenue CRM dashboard: open pipeline, weighted forecast, win rate, overdue tasks, and an insights list with suggested next actions.',
		title: 'Dashboard',
		text: 'Open pipeline, weighted forecast, and what needs attention first, on one screen.',
	},
	{
		src: '/images/crm/screen-deals-en.webp',
		alt: 'Deal kanban with Prospecting, Discovery, Proposal, and Quote columns; each card shows amount, probability, and close date.',
		title: 'Deal kanban',
		text: 'Drag deals between stages. Probability and next action update as you go.',
	},
	{
		src: '/images/crm/screen-jade-en.webp',
		alt: 'Jade, the AI agent, answering "What should I do today?" with a table of the 10 open deals and a funnel breakdown.',
		title: 'Jade, the AI agent',
		text: 'Ask in plain language. Jade aggregates, summarizes, and suggests the next move.',
	},
	{
		src: '/images/crm/screen-dashboard.webp',
		alt: 'The same dashboard in Japanese. The sidebar has a JA / EN / 繁中 language switch.',
		title: 'Three languages',
		text: 'Switch the whole UI between English, Japanese, and Traditional Chinese.',
	},
];

---

<BaseLayout
	title="Revenue CRM for B2B (Beta) | The first CRM for companies that don't have one yet"
	description="A CRM that arrives pre-configured for three business types: B2B sales, agencies and contract work, and SaaS resellers. Built for teams whose customer data still lives in spreadsheets and inboxes, with nothing to migrate. Serving individual customers instead? See the school edition. Currently in closed beta."
	lang="en"
	alternateUrl="/crm/"
>

<!-- ===================== HERO ===================== -->
<section class="hero">
	<div class="container">
		<span class="eyebrow"><span class="eyebrow__dot"></span>Product · Closed Beta</span>
		<h1>The first CRM for companies<br />that don't have one yet.<span class="hero-edition">For B2B</span></h1>
		<p class="hero-lead">
			Your customer data lives in spreadsheets and inboxes. The status of a deal lives
			in one person's head. Revenue CRM is built to start from exactly there.
			There is nothing to migrate, and nothing about the way you work today that you
			have to give up. It begins by turning what you already do in a spreadsheet into a record that stays.
		</p>
		<div class="hero-actions">
			<a href="/en/contact/" class="btn btn--hero-primary btn--lg">Apply as a beta partner →</a>
			<a href="#features" class="btn btn--hero-outline btn--lg">See features</a>
		</div>
		<p class="hero-switch">Running a school or a studio? <a href="/en/crm/school/">See the school edition →</a></p>
		<p class="hero-note">* Currently in closed beta. We are looking for a small number of partners to build this with. Features may change without notice.</p>
	</div>
</section>

<!-- ===================== POSITIONING ===================== -->
<section class="positioning">
	<div class="container">
		<div class="pos-body">
			<p class="pos-lead">
				Revenue CRM is the way of thinking about revenue structure we have used across
				40 engagements, turned into something that runs.
			</p>
			<p>
				Consilegy's consulting work <strong>starts from the tools you already have</strong>.
				If Salesforce, HubSpot, kintone, or Marketo is in place, we redesign around them
				so that investment keeps working. We do not push Revenue CRM on anyone.
			</p>
			<p>
				Revenue CRM fits companies with nothing to migrate from. No tools to evaluate
				against each other, no data to throw away. It is one option for getting from
				that starting point to "the state of every customer is on the record" by the
				shortest route available.
			</p>
			<a href="/en/services/revenue-architecture-design/" class="pos-link">Read about this approach →</a>
		</div>
	</div>
</section>

<!-- ===================== PILLARS ===================== -->
<section class="pillars">
	<div class="container">
		<div class="pillar-grid">
			<div class="pillar">
				<span class="pillar-kicker">AI-native</span>
				<h3>AI operates the CRM</h3>
				<p>Ask in plain language. Search and actions both go through. From call analysis to scoring, AI takes the busywork.</p>
			</div>
			<div class="pillar pillar--accent">
				<span class="pillar-num">103<span class="pillar-unit">flows</span></span>
				<h3>RevOps automation built in</h3>
				<p>Pre-built playbooks spanning marketing, sales, and CS. Flip a toggle and they run. Another 72 are in preparation.</p>
			</div>
			<div class="pillar">
				<span class="pillar-kicker">Clean UI</span>
				<h3>Easy enough to actually adopt</h3>
				<p>An interface that sticks with the people doing the work. Less data entry, and the data comes together on its own.</p>
			</div>
			<div class="pillar">
				<span class="pillar-kicker">日本語 / English / 繁體中文</span>
				<h3>The whole UI switches across three languages</h3>
				<p>One button changes the interface. Japanese and international members read the same data, each in their own language. Designed with Taiwan and the wider Asia region in mind.</p>
			</div>
		</div>
	</div>
</section>

<!-- ===================== DEMO VIDEO ===================== -->
<section class="demo-video">
	<div class="container">
		<div class="video-frame">
			<img
				src="/videos/revenue-crm-demo-en.gif"
				alt="A tour of Revenue CRM in the English UI. The dashboard shows open pipeline and weighted forecast, deals are viewed on a kanban board, the automation library lists 103 workflows, Jade (the AI) is asked for the funnel status and returns a lifecycle-stage breakdown, and finally the UI switches to Traditional Chinese and Japanese and back to English."
				width="880"
				height="496"
				loading="lazy"
				decoding="async"
			/>
		</div>
		<p class="video-caption">Product demo: dashboard → deal kanban → automation library → Jade (AI) → language switch.</p>
	</div>
</section>

<!-- ===================== SCREENS ===================== -->
<section class="screens" id="screens">
	<div class="container">
		<div class="feat-head">
			<p class="section-eyebrow">Screens</p>
			<h2>The numbers you look at first, and the people you move on next.</h2>
		</div>
		<ul class="screen-grid">
			{screens.map((item) => (
				<li class="screen-card">
					<figure>
						<img
							src={item.src}
							alt={item.alt}
							width="1600"
							height="1000"
							loading="lazy"
							decoding="async"
						/>
					</figure>
					<div class="screen-caption">
						<strong>{item.title}</strong>
						<span>{item.text}</span>
					</div>
				</li>
			))}
		</ul>
	</div>
</section>

<!-- ===================== EDITIONS ===================== -->
<section class="editions">
	<div class="container">
		<p class="section-eyebrow">Editions</p>
		<h2 class="ed-title">Pre-configured for the shape of your business.</h2>
		<p class="ed-lead">
			Even within one CRM, whether the thing you handle is a <em>deal</em>, a <em>project</em>,
			or a <em>contract</em> changes which screens you need and which numbers you chase.
			In Revenue CRM you pick your business type, and the terminology, screens, and
			automations switch to match. You can change it later.
		</p>
		<div class="ed-grid">
			<article class="ed-card">
				<span class="ed-tag">B2B</span>
				<h3>B2B sales</h3>
				<p class="ed-desc">The standard setup: manage prospects as deals and follow them through to closed-won.</p>
				<ul class="ed-items">
					<li>Centered on: <strong>deals</strong></li>
					<li>Pipeline, forecast, and quotes</li>
					<li>Alerts on stalled deals</li>
				</ul>
			</article>
			<article class="ed-card">
				<span class="ed-tag">Contractor</span>
				<h3>Agencies &amp; contract work</h3>
				<p class="ed-desc">For businesses running client engagements. We call them projects, not deals.</p>
				<ul class="ed-items">
					<li>Centered on: <strong>projects</strong></li>
					<li>The quote → won → delivery → invoice loop</li>
					<li>Maintenance-contract renewal dates managed automatically</li>
				</ul>
			</article>
			<article class="ed-card">
				<span class="ed-tag">Reseller</span>
				<h3>SaaS resellers</h3>
				<p class="ed-desc">For businesses where the sale is not the end and renewals are the revenue.</p>
				<ul class="ed-items">
					<li>Centered on: <strong>contracts</strong></li>
					<li>Renewal-risk scoring</li>
					<li>Churn-signal detection and automatic renewal-deal creation</li>
				</ul>
			</article>
		</div>
		<p class="ed-foot">
			For businesses built on keeping students coming back, such as schools and studios,
			there is a <a href="/en/crm/school/">school edition</a> where enrollment and retention
			take the place of deals.
		</p>
	</div>
</section>

<!-- ===================== PROBLEM ===================== -->
<section class="problem">
	<div class="container">
		<p class="section-eyebrow">Why CRM fails</p>
		<h2 class="prob-title">Sound familiar?</h2>
		<div class="prob-grid">
			<div class="prob-item">
				<p>Customer information is scattered across spreadsheets and inboxes. Nobody can tell which copy is current.</p>
			</div>
			<div class="prob-item">
				<p>Deal status lives in one person's head. Everything stops when they take a day off.</p>
			</div>
			<div class="prob-item">
				<p>Revenue is growing, but nobody can say how much will land next month.</p>
			</div>
		</div>
	</div>
</section>

<!-- ===================== FEATURES ===================== -->
<section class="features" id="features">
	<div class="container">
		<div class="feat-head">
			<p class="section-eyebrow">Features</p>
			<h2>The core of what moves revenue forward.</h2>
		</div>
		<div class="feat-grid">
			<article class="feat-card">
				<h3>AI agent</h3>
				<p>Ask your data in plain language. From drafting emails to suggesting the next action, AI takes work off the team.</p>
			</article>
			<article class="feat-card">
				<h3>Lead scoring</h3>
				<p>Promising leads surface automatically from behavior and firmographics. See who to work right now.</p>
			</article>
			<article class="feat-card">
				<h3>Workflow automation</h3>
				<p>Fire notifications, tasks, and emails on your conditions. Less manual work, and nothing slips through.</p>
			</article>
			<article class="feat-card">
				<h3>Email sequences</h3>
				<p>Multi-step follow-up sent automatically, branching on replies and behavior.</p>
			</article>
			<article class="feat-card">
				<h3>Forecasting</h3>
				<p>See where you will land straight from the pipeline, so meetings become decisions instead of status reports.</p>
			</article>
			<article class="feat-card">
				<h3>Custom objects</h3>
				<p>Extend the data model freely to fit your operations. Design it around how revenue actually flows in your business.</p>
			</article>
		</div>
	</div>
</section>

<!-- ===================== ALL FEATURES ===================== -->
<section class="all-features">
	<div class="container">
		<div class="feat-head">
			<p class="section-eyebrow">All features</p>
			<h2>Sales, marketing, CS, and ops in one place.</h2>
		</div>
		<div class="cat-grid">
			<div class="cat-card">
				<h3>AI &amp; Intelligence</h3>
				<ul>
					<li>AI assistant (search &amp; operate the CRM in plain language)</li>
					<li>AI call analysis (MEDDPICC / BANT / CHAMP / SPIN)</li>
					<li>AI research (web, with citations)</li>
					<li>AI summarization &amp; classification</li>
					<li>AI attribute fields (AI columns on records)</li>
					<li>Voice transcription (Whisper)</li>
					<li>Lead scoring (grades A–F)</li>
					<li>ICP definition → fit scoring</li>
					<li>Workspace credit management</li>
				</ul>
			</div>
			<div class="cat-card">
				<h3>CRM core</h3>
				<ul>
					<li>Contacts / Companies / Deals</li>
					<li>Tickets / Tasks / Activities / Calls</li>
					<li>Deal kanban (drag &amp; drop)</li>
					<li>Lead conversion (stage change + deal creation)</li>
					<li>Pipeline &amp; stage management</li>
					<li>Notes, attachments &amp; favorites</li>
					<li>Record-to-record relations</li>
				</ul>
			</div>
			<div class="cat-card">
				<h3>Marketing</h3>
				<ul>
					<li>Form builder (public pages, auto-create contacts)</li>
					<li>Email delivery (templates &amp; campaigns)</li>
					<li>Open / click tracking &amp; unsubscribe management</li>
					<li>Lists (static / dynamic)</li>
					<li>Workflows (visual automation)</li>
					<li>Triggers, conditional branches &amp; delay steps</li>
				</ul>
			</div>
			<div class="cat-card">
				<h3>Sales</h3>
				<ul>
					<li>Forecasting (rolled up by category)</li>
					<li>Sequences (automated multi-step follow-up)</li>
					<li>Quotes (line items, tax rates, status)</li>
					<li>Product catalog</li>
					<li>Contact roles (decision maker, champion, and more)</li>
				</ul>
			</div>
			<div class="cat-card">
				<h3>Customer Success</h3>
				<ul>
					<li>Omnichannel inbox (chat / email / API)</li>
					<li>Embeddable chat widget (real-time)</li>
					<li>Inbound email turned into conversations</li>
					<li>Knowledge base</li>
					<li>Surveys (NPS / CSAT / CES)</li>
				</ul>
			</div>
			<div class="cat-card">
				<h3>RevOps automation</h3>
				<ul>
					<li>A catalog of 103 pre-built workflows (72 more in preparation)</li>
					<li>Covers marketing / sales / CS</li>
					<li>Toggle on/off, attach sequences</li>
					<li>Issue-based nurtures &amp; stalled-deal alerts</li>
					<li>SLA escalation &amp; automatic renewal-deal creation</li>
					<li>Cross-sell candidates, business reviews &amp; more</li>
				</ul>
			</div>
			<div class="cat-card">
				<h3>Subscriptions &amp; billing</h3>
				<ul>
					<li>Edition switch (B2B sales / contractor / reseller / B2C)</li>
					<li>Subscription management</li>
					<li>Recurring metrics (MRR / ARR / churn / LTV)</li>
					<li>Stripe (customer sync, payment links, invoices)</li>
				</ul>
			</div>
			<div class="cat-card">
				<h3>Platform &amp; extensibility</h3>
				<ul>
					<li>Custom objects &amp; custom fields</li>
					<li>Record types &amp; relationship definitions</li>
					<li>REST API (v1) / GraphQL / MCP server</li>
					<li>Outbound webhooks (signed, with delivery logs)</li>
					<li>Permissions (role × CRUD) &amp; audit log</li>
					<li>Multi-workspace, member invites &amp; role management</li>
					<li>Trash (restore) &amp; global search</li>
					<li>Integrations: Notion / Google / LinkedIn</li>
					<li>Multilingual (日本語 / English / 繁體中文): the whole UI switches</li>
				</ul>
			</div>
		</div>
	</div>
</section>

<!-- ===================== ORIGIN STORY ===================== -->
<section class="origin">
	<div class="container origin-inner">
		<div class="origin-copy">
			<p class="section-eyebrow">Origin</p>
			<h2>Where this CRM was born</h2>
			<p>
				Revenue CRM did not take shape in an office in Japan. It took shape at
				<strong>Nomad Hualien (花蓮雲基地)</strong>, the digital nomad hub run by
				Hualien County, Taiwan.
			</p>
			<p>
				Seiko Yamaguchi, Consilegy's founder, was selected for the first cohort of the
				residency program. Sharing desks with founders and remote workers from across
				the region, and running cross-border meetings as a matter of routine,
				<strong>the "CRM × AI" shape</strong> emerged out of working alongside them.
			</p>
			<p>
				The thinking about revenue structure built across 40 B2B engagements in Japan
				is layered with the working practices of several countries encountered there.
				The design does not assume Japanese business customs alone, because the place
				it was born was not that kind of place.
			</p>
			<p class="origin-name">
				The AI built into the CRM is named <strong>Jade</strong> because jade is what
				Hualien is known for. It carries the name of the place it came from.
			</p>
		</div>
		<figure class="origin-quote">
			<blockquote>
				The growth of a company does not rest on cold technology alone.<br />
				Human connection, and trust in a community,<br />
				are what make a business last.
			</blockquote>
			<figcaption>
				<span class="origin-who">Seiko Yamaguchi, Founder, Consilegy</span>
				<a
					href="https://www.seenews.com.tw/news_data.php?news_id=2325&amp;k_code=A"
					target="_blank"
					rel="noopener noreferrer"
					class="origin-src"
				>See News (花蓮視新聞), 25 June 2026: "花蓮雲基地第二季名單揭曉 日籍首季進駐者讚爆" →</a>
			</figcaption>
			<a
				href="https://www.seenews.com.tw/news_data.php?news_id=2325&amp;k_code=A"
				target="_blank"
				rel="noopener noreferrer"
				class="origin-clip"
			>
				<img
					src="/images/common/seenews-hualien-2026.jpg"
					alt="A See News (花蓮視新聞) article from 25 June 2026 reporting that Seiko, from Japan, developed a new product combining CRM and AI as a first-cohort resident of Nomad Hualien."
					width="1000"
					height="1026"
					loading="lazy"
				/>
				<span class="origin-clip__cap">From the See News (花蓮視新聞) article of 25 June 2026</span>
			</a>
		</figure>
	</div>
</section>

<!-- ===================== BETA NOTE ===================== -->
<section class="beta-band">
	<div class="container beta-inner">
		<div>
			<p class="section-eyebrow">Closed Beta</p>
			<h2>We're taking on our first customers now.</h2>
			<p class="beta-lead">
				Revenue CRM is being built as a closed beta. Companies who come on board get
				onboarding informed by Consilegy's revenue-design work, plus priority support
				where feature requests go straight into the product.
			</p>
		</div>
		<ul class="beta-list">
			<li>Hands-on setup and data migration support</li>
			<li>Advice on revenue operations design</li>
			<li>Priority on your feature requests</li>
			<li>Preferential terms during the beta</li>
		</ul>
	</div>
</section>

<!-- ===================== FINAL CTA ===================== -->
<section class="final-cta">
	<div class="container cta-inner">
		<div>
			<p class="cta-eyebrow">Get Started</p>
			<h2>We're looking for partners<br />to build this with.</h2>
			<p class="cta-lead">
				A closed beta is not the stage where a finished product gets sold. It is the
				stage where you use it in real operations, tell us what is missing, and we
				finish it together. In exchange, you get to set the priority of what we build next.
			</p>
			<div class="cta-actions">
				<a href="/en/contact/" class="btn btn--cta-primary btn--lg">Apply as a beta partner →</a>
				<a href="/en/services/" class="btn btn--cta-outline btn--lg">Already have a CRM?</a>
			</div>
		</div>
		<div class="cta-card">
			<h4>What we'll show you</h4>
			<ul class="cta-list">
				<li>The AI agent working on and suggesting actions from your data</li>
				<li>Lead scoring and prioritization</li>
				<li>Workflow and email-sequence automation</li>
				<li>Pipeline and forecast visibility</li>
				<li>Customization examples for your operations</li>
			</ul>
		</div>
	</div>
</section>

</BaseLayout>

<style>
/* ── Container ───────────────────────────────────────────
   EN サイトは global.css で --container: 72ch（読み物用の狭い段）になっている。
   このLPはカードを3列に並べるので、JA版と同じ 1120px に戻す。
   ページスコープなので他のENページには影響しない。 */
.container { max-width: 1120px; }

/* ── Shared ──────────────────────────────────────────── */
.section-eyebrow {
	font-size: 0.8125rem; font-weight: 600; color: var(--color-primary);
	letter-spacing: 0.08em; text-transform: uppercase; margin: 0 0 0.75rem;
}
.btn--lg { padding: 1.0625rem 1.875rem; font-size: 1rem; }

/* ── Hero ──────────────────────────────────────────── */
.hero {
	background: linear-gradient(180deg, var(--color-bg-subtle) 0%, var(--color-bg) 100%);
	border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border);
	padding-block: var(--space-2xl) var(--space-xl);
}
.eyebrow {
	display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.5rem;
	font-size: 0.8125rem; font-weight: 600; color: var(--color-primary);
	background: rgba(30,64,175,0.08); padding: 0.375rem 0.875rem; border-radius: 4px;
	letter-spacing: 0.05em; text-transform: uppercase; margin-bottom: 1.25rem;
}
.eyebrow__dot { width: 6px; height: 6px; border-radius: 50%; background: var(--color-primary); display: inline-block; }
.hero h1 {
	font-size: clamp(2.25rem, 4vw, 3.25rem); font-weight: 600;
	letter-spacing: 0.01em; margin: 0 0 1rem; color: var(--color-text); line-height: 1.25;
}
.hero-lead { font-size: 1.125rem; line-height: 1.8; color: var(--color-text-muted); max-width: 720px; margin: 0 0 2rem; }
.hero-actions { display: flex; gap: 0.75rem; flex-wrap: wrap; }
.hero-note { font-size: 0.8125rem; color: var(--color-text-muted); margin: 0.75rem 0 0; }

.btn--hero-primary {
	display: inline-flex; align-items: center;
	background: var(--color-primary); color: #fff;
	padding: 1.0625rem 1.875rem; border-radius: var(--radius);
	font-weight: 700; font-size: 1rem; text-decoration: none; border: none;
	transition: background 0.15s ease;
}
.btn--hero-primary:hover { background: var(--color-primary-dark); color: #fff; }
.btn--hero-outline {
	display: inline-flex; align-items: center;
	background: transparent; color: var(--color-primary);
	padding: 1.0625rem 1.875rem; border-radius: var(--radius);
	font-weight: 600; font-size: 1rem; text-decoration: none;
	border: 1.5px solid var(--color-primary);
	transition: all 0.15s ease;
}
.btn--hero-outline:hover { background: rgba(30,64,175,0.06); }

/* ── Pillars ───────────────────────────────────────── */
.pillars { padding-block: var(--space-xl); background: var(--color-bg); }
/* 英文は日本語のように任意の位置で折り返せないため、JA版の4カラムではなく2×2にする */
.pillar-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr); gap: 1.25rem; }
.pillar {
	border: 1px solid var(--color-border); border-radius: var(--radius-card);
	padding: 2rem; background: var(--color-bg-subtle);
}
.pillar--accent {
	background: linear-gradient(180deg, #f7faff 0%, var(--color-bg) 70%);
	border-color: color-mix(in oklch, var(--color-primary), transparent 70%);
}
.pillar-kicker {
	display: inline-block; font-size: 0.75rem; font-weight: 700; color: var(--color-primary);
	letter-spacing: 0.08em; text-transform: uppercase; margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
}
.pillar-num {
	display: block; font-size: 3rem; font-weight: 700; line-height: 1;
	color: var(--color-primary); letter-spacing: -0.02em; margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
}
